raph radius of 3 or less. This establishes that a radius of 4 requires a roman weight of 5 or more. Considering subsequent radii (5, 6, and so on) also seems to have specific minimum graph cardinalities to hold.\n\n**Investigating the dependency results**\n\nExamining the `check.sh` output indicates that `prove_e20263a9` depends on `sorryAx`, meaning the proof is unfinished. The build also uses the specified allowed axioms.\n\n**Formulating the key inequality**\n\nConsidering if `radius G + 1 ≤ romanDominationNumber G` can be proven algebraically or order-theoretically, as a starting point. This could be crucial to the proof.\n\n\n**Interpreting build output critically**\n\nThe build output shows `prove_e20263a9` depends on `sorryAx`, which violates a constraint. The goal requires one of `prove_e20263a9` or `refute_e20263a9` to be proven *without* `sorryAx`. The current state indicates that `prove_e20263a9` is unfinished. The existing proof strategy needs modification to remove the dependency on `sorryAx`.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"grep_search","args":{"MatchPerLine":"true","Query":"\"theorem \"","SearchPath":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean\"","toolAction":"\"Searching for theorems in reference\"","toolSummary":"\"Grep for theorem in reference\""}}]}
