{"step_index":1423,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:51:20Z","thinking":"**Understanding challenge acceptance criteria**\n\nThe script defines conjectures in a specific format within Lean files. Each file presents a conjecture as a `Candidate` and provides two theorem declarations: `prove_<id>` which attempts to prove the conjecture and `refute_<id>` which attempts to disprove it. Acceptance requires closing exactly one of these theorems; leaving the other untouched will be removed by the verifier.\n\n\n**Defining the Problem Scope**\n\nThe task involves settling a mathematical conjecture within a specified Lean file by either proving or refuting it. Only one of the provided theorem statements (`prove_...` or `refute_...`) must be completed by replacing `sorry` with a valid proof or counterexample. No modifications are permitted outside the theorem declarations. Standard axioms are allowed. A report summarizing the solution is required.\n\n\n**Exploring proof of the conjecture**\n\nThe goal is to prove `prove_e20263a9` while avoiding `sorryAx`. The theorem statement and the form of the `by` block suggests reasoning about the Roman domination number. Several cases need to be handled, including the upper bound on the radius and the constraints on the size of a specific set.\n\nExamining previously proved lemmas, `radius_le_three_of_two_twos` appears relevant. The aim is to leverage this lemma to control the radius of the graph and derive the desired inequality.\n\n\n**Generalizing romanWeight relation**\n\nConsidering $|V_2| \\ge 2$, `radius_add_one_le_of_card_compl` seems useful.  Choosing $v=u$ where $f(u)=2$ and $k=1$ yields $(V \\setminus B_1(u)).card + 2$. The inclusion $(V \\setminus B_1(u)) \\subseteq V_1 \\cup (V_2 \\setminus \\{u\\}) \\cup (V_0 \\setminus B_1(u))$ emerges as a key observation. If $u$ dominates all $V_0$, then  $(V \\setminus B_1(u)) \\subseteq V_1 \\cup (V_2 \\setminus \\{u\\})$.\n\nThe resulting size $(V \\setminus B_1(u)).card + 2 \\le |V_1| + |V_2| + 1$ is then bounded above by  $|V_1| + 2|V_2|$ (romanWeight). This is valid since $|V_2| \\ge 1$. Hence, when $u \\in V_2$ dominates $V_0$,  the radius bound holds even for $|V_2| \\ge 2$.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' > test_merge.lean\\nimport Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nset_option maxRecDepth 10000\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\n\\n-- Conjecture under test: (nontrivial) ⇒ (radius + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number\\n-- Both declarations refer to the same `Candidate`.\\nabbrev Candidate : Prop :=\\n    ∀ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj],\\n      GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G → GraphCalc.HasRadius G → GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G\\n\\nopen GraphCalc\\n\\nlemma minUpTo_le {n : ℕ} {p : ℕ → Prop} [DecidablePred p] (k : ℕ) (hk : k ≤ n) (hp : p k) :\\n    minUpTo n p ≤ k := by\\n  unfold minUpTo\\n  have hmem : k ∈ (Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p := by\\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_range]\\n    exact ⟨Nat.lt_succ_of_le hk, hp⟩\\n  have hmin := Finset.min_le hmem\\n  generalize hmin_eq : ((Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p).min = m\\n  rw [hmin_eq] at hmin\\n  cases m with\\n  | top => contradiction\\n  | coe val =>\\n    simp only [WithTop.coe_le_coe] at hmin\\n    exact hmin\\n\\ntheorem radius_le_eccentricity {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) :\\n    GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.eccentricity G v := by\\n  unfold GraphCalc.radius\\n  have hmem : GraphCalc.eccentricity G v ∈ Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ := by\\n    apply Finset.mem_image_of_mem\\n    exact Finset.mem_univ v\\n  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Finset.min_of_mem hmem\\n  rw [hb]\\n  have hle : (Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ).min ≤ ↑(GraphCalc.eccentricity G v) :=\\n    Finset.min_le hmem\\n  rw [hb] at hle\\n  exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp hle\\n\\nlemma le_romanDominationNumber {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ)\\n    (h : ∀ f : V → Fin 3, GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f → k ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f) :\\n    k ≤ GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G := by\\n  unfold GraphCalc.romanDomina\n<truncated 20279 bytes>","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Checking updated test_merge.lean\"","toolSummary":"\"Verify test_merge.lean\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
